[00:05.08] I'd give anything to go back
[00:08.18] Days I was young.
[00:11.78] All the way back to Pan Bowl
[00:16.38] I sit down on the lakebed
[00:20.20] Stare at the sun.
[00:23.26] Then I'd walk out in the water
[00:25.94] Let it cleanse my soul.
[00:29.70] Spend my days up on quicksand
[00:33.22] There I would play.
[00:37.52] Wild as a rattlesnake
[00:40.04] Right from the start.
[00:43.12] I'd push August in
[00:46.20] Swing all day.
[00:49.80] Well she was the first girl that ever broke my heart.
[00:56.02] Miss the days when this old life
[00:58.64] Free from all the pain and strife.
[01:01.98] And all the sorrow it has brung.
[01:06.70] I'd give anything to go
[01:09.16] All the way back to Pan Bowl.
[01:12.06] All the way back to days when I was young.
[01:17.34] Spend my summers hearing stories
[01:22.56] Bout the one that got away.
[01:26.48] On a dock down at Watt's bar
[01:28.84] Every 4th of July.
[01:32.70] Uncle Everett was the coolest.
[01:35.92] Never had a word to say.
[01:39.56] When he died was the only time
[01:41.92] I ever seen papaw cry.
[01:45.86] Every Sunday we'd go visit
[01:48.58] My great-grandma Mary Ann.
[01:52.42] Lord I cry just thinking
[01:55.08] About how good she was to me.
[01:59.08] My great-grandad Eli
[02:01.68] Was a coal-mining man.
[02:06.06] Not a tooth in his head
[02:08.30] But his eyes held the sea.
[02:12.14] Miss the days when this old life
[02:14.82] Was free from my old pain and strife.
[02:18.06] And all the sorrow it has brung.
[02:22.72] I'd give anything to go
[02:25.38] All the way back to Pan Bowl.
[02:28.34] All the way back to days when I was young.
